One more thing:  Gauntlets of Power are occasionally available
rather earlier in the game.  This is especially significant for roles
like Tourist who would otherwise take rather longer to get their
strength up to 18, let alone 18/**.  These are the roles that can
really benefit from the GoP, because it lets them wear armor
that they otherwise could not (like, say, mail) and still carry
more weapons and food and tools and other survival gear than
they could otherwise manage even without the heavy armor.

It hardly matters for strong roles like Valkyrie.  Woo, you can
throw Mjollnir (as if you'd even want that, when Valkyries start
with a long sword and can advance to expert in it) and can
maybe carry 2% more or something like that.

But for roles that start with single-digit strength and low hit
points and have to keep retreating back up to level one to
heal so many times they're in serious danger of starvation,
early Gauntlets of Power are a major game-changing item.
Suddenly you can throw your darts more than three tiles,
and when you hit things with the orcish dagger you picked
up the damage you do doesn't get rounded off to zero.
You can pick up and wear armor and not be Burdened.
It's like a whole different game.


